    "reply": "The genes associated with cystic fibrosis are NCBIGene:1080 (CF transmembrane conductance regulator), NCBIGene:2212 (Fc gamma receptor IIa), and NCBIGene:7040 (transforming growth factor beta 1) [1][3][4].\n\n## Disease Context\n\nCystic fibrosis is represented in MedGen as Cystic fibrosis [6], with clinical features including asthma [11], bronchiectasis [15], clubbing of fingers [19], dehydration [23], diarrhea [27], hemoptysis [28], hepatomegaly [29], and hepatosplenomegaly [30]. The condition is also indexed in literature databases under the entity name Cystic Fibrosis [7].\n\n## Literature Findings\n\nPublications addressing cystic fibrosis span multiple clinical aspects. Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis [5] describes a rare neurological complication, specifically hyperammonemic encephalopathy precipitated in previously stable cystic fibrosis liver disease by various triggers including systemic corticosteroids [26]. Nutritional management is covered in 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis [10], while pediatric perspectives appear in Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children [14]. Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis [18] addresses antimicrobial therapy, and Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes [22] covers endocrine complications. Publication identifiers include pmid 32800451 [9], pmid 35240644 [13], pmid 35592838 [17], pmid 35853636 [21], and pmid 39129918 [25].\n\n## Clinical Trials\n\nTrials specifically for cystic fibrosis include Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [8] and Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [24]. Other trials retrieved share the term fibrocystic but target distinct conditions: A Study of Topical Danazol for the Treatment of Pain Associated With Fibrocystic Breast Disease [12], Efficacy and Safety of ONCOXIN in Patients With Breast Fibrocystic Disease [16], and A Clinical Study on the Efficacy and Safety of the Treatment of Hyperplasia of Mammary Glands With Xiaoru Sanjie Capsule [20].",
    "dur": 18.416
   }
